    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. And what's so unfortunate is the Republican Party is starting to lose its brand as the party of fiscal responsibility, trying to be Democrat and I am tired of it. And I'm frustrated. I don't know that I have a plan to leave as much as I have a plan to try to make sure that my voice is heard in as many ways as possible and to make sure that other Republicans recognize that this is a really bad strategy to try to be just like the Democrats. Anytime we suggest $1 billion in the spending that the Democrats will say that we are heartless and want to spend $2 billion, they will always outspend us. The only way we can win is to make sure Americans understand that this constant increase in the national debt just can't continue.",
