    "turn_text": "So I think it's clear that there are experts like Dr. Fauci and others who know the best way to combat this coronavirus, this pandemic that we're faced with. What they don't know is the overall effect on the economy and the overall effect on our society. Our suicide rates are increasing. Our domestic violent rates are increasing. Our substance abuse rates are increasing. Our child abuse rates are increasing. We have all these societal pathologies that are on the rise as a result of the strategy to deal with this disease. We know that this disease is while it makes people sick. It is not deadly for 99% of the population. So we need to isolate the 1% of the population and we need to address that. But we need to get our economy up and going again. When we look at Europe and we see that Europe, Germany, France, other countries have their kids in school and actually graduating this year from school. as well as planning on opening next year. When we see that they say, you know, we're going to, we recognize that 70% of our population is going to end up with this disease and we have to make sure that we protect those who are the most vulnerable. That's the strategy that America needs to look at and make sure that we're doing everything we can to produce the revenue, to have the GDP that we need so that when the tax revenue comes in, we have the resources to deal with many of these issues. We can't just keep going more and more debt because we want to give people time away from social interaction at the same time. We are giving benefits to",
