    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "And what I think is the left has always tried to attack our values and they have always denied what a great country this is and the reasons for our greatness. The fact that we have this Constitution that grants people certain rights, the fact that our founding fathers flawed as they were, were great Americans who understood that the relationship between the government and the people can be fundamentally changed from what it was throughout history. And that's really what America stands for. And so while we are under attack, I think most Americans recognize that this is a darn good country, the best in the world. And if we continue down the path of respecting individuals and having a compassionate government that helps lift people out of poverty and really a private sector that creates the job opportunities to lift people out of poverty, we will continue to be a great country if we deny our history. We try to change our history. if we tear down statutes, if we burn stores, we get nowhere. And that's just not a good",
