    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86197.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "It is and especially since the governors of the 50 states are the primary responders to this virus. They decided how to shut down their economies. They decided how much to test and when to test and who to test. The decision makers are at a lower level of government and now the Democrats have nothing to do but point their finger at this president and try to make him appear to be responsible for this. This president has done everything he can in terms of economic policy that has helped people in this country, helped businesses in this country. He has made sure that as quickly as this country could respond with tests and other things we did respond. And yet the idea that somehow this president is responsible for deaths is just it's petty politics in an election year. And I don't believe the American people are buying into it.",
