    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86197.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "I couldn't agree with you more, Congressman, but I'm going to jump over to the elections because I know I have you for only a certain amount of time. I want to talk a little bit about, first of all, Colorado. Tell me what the feeling is there, what is your feeling from your home state of Colorado, and then I want to ask you about Joe Biden. Right now, there's an article that just came out today in the New York Times. New York Times is pushing for basically so that Joe Biden does not debate President Trump live. No debates. That's what they're arguing. They're arguing for absolutely no debates. We know the reason why. We know that there's issues with, unfortunately, I believe, with former Vice President Joe Biden, his ability to retain certain memories of things. And we've seen that. But this is a pretty big deal, absolutely no debate. I mean, are you for that? What do you think's going on here?",
